    type "POI"
    name "P&#232;re Lachaise Cemetery"
    category "history"
    lat 48.861111
    lon 2.394167
    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.97
    description "P&#232;re Lachaise Cemetery (French: Cimeti&#232;re du P&#232;re-Lachaise [simtj&#603;&#641; dy p&#603;&#641; la&#643;&#603;&#720;z], formerly Cimeti&#232;re de l'Est, lit. 'Cemetery of the East') is the largest cemetery in Paris, France, at 44 hectares (110 acres). The P&#232;re Lachaise is located in the 20th arrondissement and was the first garden cemetery, as well as the first municipal cemetery in Paris. It is also the site of three World War I memorials. The cemetery is located on the Boulevard de M&#233;nilmontant."
    destination_id "PAR"
    open_hour 8
    close_hour 17
    opening_hours_raw "Mo-Fr 08:00-17:30; Sa 08:30-17:30; Su 09:00-17:30"
  ]
  node [
    id 6
    label "POI0006"
    type "POI"
    name "Montmartre"
    category "nature"
    lat 48.886944
    lon 2.341111
    avg_visit_minutes 90
    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.96
    description "Montmartre (UK: mon-MAR-tr&#601;, US: mohn-, French: [m&#596;&#771;martr] ) is a large hill in Paris's northern 18th arrondissement. It is 130 m (430 ft) high and gives its name to the surrounding district, part of the Right Bank. Montmartre is primarily known for its artistic history, for the white-domed Basilica of the Sacr&#233;-C&#339;ur on its summit, and as a nightclub district. The other church on the hill, Saint Pierre de Montmartre, built in 1147, was the church of the prestigious Montmartre Abbey."
    destination_id "PAR"
    open_hour 0
    close_hour 24
    opening_hours_raw ""
  ]
  node [
