    avg_visit_minutes 90
    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.86
    description "The &#206;le de la Cit&#233; (French: [il d(&#601;) la site]; lit. &#34;Island of the City&#34;) is one of two natural islands on the Seine River (alongside &#206;le Saint-Louis) in central Paris. It spans 22.5 hectares (56 acres) of land. In the 4th century, it was the site of the fortress of the area governor for the Roman Empire. In 508, Clovis I, the first King of the Franks, established his palace on the island."
    destination_id "PAR"
