    name "Catacombs of Paris"
    category "museum"
    lat 48.83397
    lon 2.33245
    avg_visit_minutes 120
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.95
    description "The Catacombs of Paris (French: Catacombes de Paris, ) are underground ossuaries in Paris, France, which hold the remains of more than six million people. Built to consolidate Paris's ancient stone quarries, they extend south from the Barri&#232;re d'Enfer (&#34;Gate of Hell&#34;) former city gate. The ossuary was created as part of the effort to eliminate the effects of the city's overflowing cemeteries."
    destination_id "PAR"
    open_hour 9
    close_hour 20
    opening_hours_raw "Tu-Su 09:45-20:30"
  ]
