    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.8
    description "The Champ de Mars is a large public greenspace in Paris, France, located in the seventh arrondissement, between the Eiffel Tower to the northwest and the &#201;cole Militaire to the southeast. The park is named after the Campus Martius (&#34;Mars Field&#34;) in Rome, which was dedicated to the god Mars. The name alludes to the fact that the lawns here were formerly used as drilling and marching grounds by the French military."
    destination_id "PAR"
