    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.91
    description "The Place de la Concorde (French: [plas d(&#601;) la k&#596;&#771;k&#596;&#641;d] ; &#34;Harmony Square&#34;), originally the Place Louis XV (Louis XV Square), and later the Place Louis XVI (Louis XVI Square), is a public square in Paris. Measuring 7.6 ha (19 acres) in area, it is the largest square in the city. It is located in the 8th arrondissement, at the eastern end of the Champs-&#201;lys&#233;es."
