    popularity_score 4.91
    description "The Palais Garnier (French: [pal&#603; &#609;a&#641;nje] , &#34;Garnier Palace&#34;), also known as Op&#233;ra Garnier (French: [&#596;pe&#641;a &#609;a&#641;nje] , &#34;Garnier Opera&#34;), is a historic 1,979-seat opera house at the Place de l'Op&#233;ra in the 9th arrondissement of Paris, France. It was built for the Paris Opera from 1861 to 1875 at the behest of Emperor Napoleon III."
    destination_id "PAR"
