    lon 2.345028
    avg_visit_minutes 30
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.89
    description "The Sainte-Chapelle (French: [s&#603;&#771;t &#643;ap&#603;l]; English: Holy Chapel) is a royal chapel in the Gothic style, within the medieval Palais de la Cit&#233;, the residence of the Kings of France until the 14th century, on the &#206;le de la Cit&#233; in the River Seine in Paris, France. Construction began sometime after 1238 and the chapel was consecrated on 26 April 1248. The Sainte-Chapelle is considered among the highest achievements of the Rayonnant period of Gothic architecture."
    destination_id "PAR"
    open_hour 9
