    avg_visit_minutes 120
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.87
    description "The Centre Pompidou (French pronunciation: [s&#593;&#771;t&#641; p&#596;&#771;pidu]), more fully the Centre national d'art et de culture Georges-Pompidou (lit. 'Georges Pompidou National Centre of Art and Culture'), also known as the Pompidou Centre in English and colloquially as Beaubourg, is a building complex in Paris, France. It was designed in the style of high-tech architecture by the architectural team of Richard Rogers, Su Rogers and Renzo Piano, along with Gianfranco Franchini."
