    description "The Closerie des Lilas (French pronunciation: [kloz&#641;i de lila]) is a famous Parisian restaurant (or brasserie) located on the Boulevard du Montparnasse in the 6th arrondissement of Paris. It was opened in 1847 by Fran&#231;ois Bullier and was a simple brasserie at the beginning. Initially, it was named after a theatre piece called La Closerie des Genets by Fr&#233;d&#233;ric Souli&#233;. It progressively evolved into the Closerie des Lilas because its owner, Bullier, used to plant lilac flowers."
    destination_id "PAR"
