    description "The Mus&#233;e de l'Arm&#233;e (French: [myze d&#601; la&#641;me]; &#34;Army Museum&#34;) is a national military museum of France located at Les Invalides in the 7th arrondissement of Paris. It is served by Paris M&#233;tro stations Invalides, Varenne and La Tour-Maubourg The Mus&#233;e de l'Arm&#233;e was created in 1905 with the merger of the Mus&#233;e d'Artillerie and the Mus&#233;e Historique de l'Arm&#233;e. The museum's seven main spaces and departments contain collections that span the period from antiquity through the 20th century."
