    description "The Gare Saint-Lazare (French pronunciation: [&#609;a&#641; s&#603;&#771; laza&#641;]; lit. 'Saint Lazarus station'), officially Paris Saint Lazare, is one of the seven large mainline railway station terminals in Paris, France. It was the first railway station built in Paris, opening in 1837. It mostly serves train services to western suburbs, as well as intercity services toward Normandy using the Paris&#8211;Le Havre railway. Saint-Lazare is the third busiest station in France, after the Gare du Nord and Gare de Lyon."
