    description "The Pont de Bir-Hakeim (French: [p&#596;&#771; d(&#601;) bi&#641;ak&#603;m]; English: Bir Hakeim Bridge), is a steel open spandrel deck arch bridge on stone masonry starlings, which crosses the Seine in Paris, France. The bridge is named after the 1942 battle in Libya; until 1948 it was known as the Pont de Passy ([p&#596;&#771; d(&#601;) pasi]; Passy Bridge). The Pont de Bir-Hakeim connects the 15th and 16th arrondissements, passing over the northeast end of the &#206;le aux Cygnes (Isle of the Swans)."
    destination_id "PAR"
    open_hour 8
