    description "The Canal Saint-Denis (French pronunciation: [kanal s&#603;&#771; d&#601;ni]) is a 6.6-kilometre-long (4.1 mi) canal in Paris, France. The canal connects the Canal de l'Ourcq, at a point north-northwest of the Bassin de la Villette in the 19th arrondissement, with the suburban municipalities of Saint-Denis and Aubervilliers in the department of Seine-Saint-Denis. There are seven locks along the canal's route, and, near Saint-Denis, the canal discharges into the Seine."
