    description "The Op&#233;ra-Comique (French pronunciation: [&#596;pe&#641;a k&#596;mik]) is a Paris opera company which was founded around 1714 by some of the popular theatres of the Parisian fairs. In 1762 the company was merged with &#8211; and for a time took the name of &#8211; its chief rival, the Com&#233;die-Italienne at the H&#244;tel de Bourgogne. It was also called the Th&#233;&#226;tre-Italien up to about 1793, when it again became most commonly known as the Op&#233;ra-Comique."
