    avg_visit_minutes 90
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.04
    description "The Rive Droite (French: [&#641;iv d&#641;wat]; French for 'Right Bank') is most commonly associated with the river Seine in central Paris. Here, the river flows roughly westwards, cutting the city into two parts. When facing downstream, the northern bank is to the right, whereas the southern bank (or Rive Gauche) is to the left. The Rive Droite's most famous street is the Champs-&#201;lys&#233;es, with others of prominence being the Rue de la Paix, Rue de Rivoli, Avenue de l'Op&#233;ra and Avenue Montaigne."
    destination_id "PAR"
