    description "The Cr&#233;merie-Restaurant Polidor is a historic restaurant in the 6th arrondissement of Paris open 365 days a year. Its predecessor was a cheese shop founded in 1845 and the cr&#233;merie part of its name derives from the French cheese, eggs and cream it first sold as a fromagerie. In 1890 the owner changed it into a bistro restaurant. It has had its present name since the beginning of the 20th century."
