    description "&#201;glise Saint-Eug&#232;ne-Sainte-C&#233;cile is a Roman Catholic church located at 6 rue Sainte-C&#233;cile in the 9th arrondissement of Paris. In 1983 it was designated as a monument historique in its entirety. Designed in the Neo-Gothic style by Louis-Auguste Boileau and Louis-Adrien Lusson, the church was the first in France to use an entirely iron-framed construction. The first stone was laid in 1854, and the building was completed in 1855."
    destination_id "PAR"
