    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.01
    description "The Trocad&#233;ro Palace was an eclectic building of Moorish and neo-Byzantine inspiration dating from the second half of the 19th century. Located in the 16th arrondissement of Paris, on the Convent of the Visitandines de Chaillot between the Place du Trocad&#233;ro and the gardens of the same name, it comprised a 4,600-seat auditorium extended on either side by two curved wings, each housing a museum (the Mus&#233;e des Monuments Fran&#231;ais and the Mus&#233;e d'Ethnographie), as well as conference rooms."
    destination_id "PAR"
