    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.96
    description "The Fernsehturm (German: [&#712;f&#603;&#865;&#601;nze&#720;&#716;t&#650;&#865;&#592;m] ; lit. 'Television Tower') in central Berlin was constructed between 1965 and 1969 by the government of the German Democratic Republic as both a functional broadcasting facility and a symbol of communist power. It remains a landmark today from its position next to Alexanderplatz in the city's Marien Quarter, part of the district of Mitte, visible across most suburban districts of Berlin."
    destination_id "BER"
    open_hour 8
    close_hour 19
    opening_hours_raw ""
