    avg_visit_minutes 30
    price_level 0
    popularity_score 4.67
    description "St. Hedwig's Cathedral (German: St.-Hedwigs-Kathedrale) is the Catholic cathedral of the Archdiocese of Berlin on Bebelplatz in the historic centre of Berlin. Dedicated in honor of Hedwig of Silesia, it was erected from 1747 to 1773 by order of Frederick the Great according to plans by Georg Wenzeslaus von Knobelsdorff in Baroque style."
    destination_id "BER"
    open_hour 10
    close_hour 17
    opening_hours_raw "Mo-Sa 10:00-17:00; Su 13:00-17:00; PH off"
