    description "The Berlin Palace (German: Berliner Schloss), formerly known as the Royal Palace (German: K&#246;nigliches Schloss), is a large building adjacent to Berlin Cathedral and the Museum Island in the Mitte area of Berlin. It was the main residence of the Electors of Brandenburg, Kings of Prussia and German Emperors from 1443 to 1918."
    destination_id "BER"
    open_hour 8
