    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 4.86
    description "The Volkshalle (German pronunciation: [&#712;f&#596;lks&#716;hal&#601;], &#34;People's Hall&#34;), also called Gro&#223;e Halle ([&#716;&#609;&#641;o&#720;s&#601; &#712;hal&#601;], &#34;Great Hall&#34;) or Ruhmeshalle ([&#712;&#641;u&#720;m&#601;s&#716;hal&#601;], &#34;Hall of Glory&#34;), was a proposal for a monumental, domed building to be built in a reconstituted Berlin (renamed as Germania) in Nazi Germany. The project was conceived by Adolf Hitler and designed by his architect Albert Speer. No part of the building was ever constructed. The word Volk had a particular resonance in Nazi thinking."
    destination_id "BER"
