    lon 13.379278
    avg_visit_minutes 120
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 3.39
    description "The Berlin Spy Museum is a private museum in Berlin which was created by former journalist Franz-Michael G&#252;nther. The museum opened to the public on 19 September 2015. G&#252;nther's aspirations were to create a museum devoted to the history of spies and espionage in the former spy capital of Germany. The museum is located in the central area of Potsdamer Platz, formerly known as the &#34;death strip&#34;, as it lies on the perimeters of the wall which once divided East and West Berlin."
    destination_id "BER"
