    lon 13.401111
    avg_visit_minutes 60
    price_level 1
    popularity_score 3.68
    description "Rosenthaler Platz is a Berlin U-Bahn station located on the U8. Opened on 18 April 1930, the station was designed by Alfred Grenander, making prominent use of orange uranium tiles. From 1961 to 1989 the station was one of the city's many &#34;ghost stations&#34;. The station served as a temporary border crossing after the fall of the Berlin Wall."
    destination_id "BER"
    open_hour 8
